WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.355
A useful AI homelab needs basic operations habits.

00:00:03.355 --> 00:00:09.393
Monitor temperature, power, disk usage, memory, GPU utilization, service health, and logs.

00:00:09.393 --> 00:00:14.157
AI workloads can stress hardware in ways ordinary desktop use does not.

00:00:14.157 --> 00:00:21.806
High temperatures, full disks, driver crashes, runaway notebooks, and failed services can make the lab unreliable.

00:00:21.806 --> 00:00:26.905
Monitoring gives you early warning before a small problem becomes a rebuild.

00:00:26.905 --> 00:00:29.522
Model inventory is part of maintenance.

00:00:29.522 --> 00:00:40.726
Keep track of which models are installed, where they came from, what license or use restrictions apply, what quantization they use, and which workflows depend on them.

00:00:40.726 --> 00:00:46.765
Without inventory, the model directory becomes a pile of large files with unclear purpose.

00:00:46.765 --> 00:00:52.401
Good inventory helps with cleanup, troubleshooting, comparison, and responsible use.

00:00:52.401 --> 00:00:55.085
Dependency updates should be deliberate.

00:00:55.085 --> 00:01:03.539
AI tooling changes quickly, and a working stack can break after a driver, Python package, container image, or frontend update.

00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:10.315
Configuration backups, version notes, and rollback planning keep updates from becoming one-way trips.

00:01:10.315 --> 00:01:21.922
If an upgrade fails, decide whether to troubleshoot or rebuild based on the value of the current environment, the quality of documentation, and the time required to recover.

00:01:21.922 --> 00:01:24.472
Experiment notes are operational data.

00:01:24.472 --> 00:01:31.383
Record what you changed, what model you tested, what parameters mattered, what worked, and what failed.

00:01:31.383 --> 00:01:34.603
This turns random trial and error into learning.

00:01:34.603 --> 00:01:38.830
Over time, the lab should become more useful, not more fragile.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:42.118
Maintenance is not separate from experimentation.

00:01:42.118 --> 00:01:45.070
It is what keeps experimentation repeatable.
